What is a Prosthetic Foot?
Prosthetic feet are sophisticated medical devices that replicate the function of the human foot. They incorporate features such as energy storage and return, shock absorption, multi-axial rotation, and adjustable heel heights to enable a wide range of activities from daily walking to specialized sports.
